,[132.88,133.43,130.3,131.44,1063200],[132.56,132.73,129.57,129.62,802300],[128.14,130.44,127.73,130.31,955600]],"about":{"what":"Stanley Black & Decker (SWK). This chart runs from Apr 23, 2019 to Aug 28, 2019.","setup":"The stock rose about 22% in the three months before the base, a bit under the 30% that marks a classic setup. It then formed a base for about 11 weeks, peaking at $153.26 and pulling back 17% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jul 24, 2019 it closed at $152.51, its first close above the base high of $152.46. Volume that day was 2.6M shares, 1.92x the prior 10-day average of 1.3M. It didn't hold. By Jul 29, 2019 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $130.31.","lesson":"This is an example of a failed breakout where everything looked right, volume included, and the stock fell back anyway. It happens. This is why traders cut losses fast instead of hoping."}}